WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
FCC clears 15,000 new starlink satellites, enabling direct competition in wireless service. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 123. The Federal Communications Commission granted approval on October 6th for SpaceX to launch and operate 15,000 next generation satellites dedicated to Starlink mobile. That decision arrived about a year after the original filing from September 2025. The commission also issued a wait

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.500
that Let's Space X provide wireless service directly through satellites, without first leasing

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:42.280
spectrum from a ground-based operator. Space X expects the new satellites to deliver up to 150

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:50.380
megabits per second to each user. They will fly between 326 and 335 kilometers altitude to keep

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:56.660
latency low. The frequencies come from bands acquired from Echo Star, and testing on those bands

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:02.620
is allowed only until the second stage of that acquisition closes on November 30, 2027.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:09.240
SpaceX plans to start launching the second-generation mobile satellites before that deadline arrives.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.940
Notebook check covered the full regulatory details. SpaceX also released fresh orbital footage

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:21.760
from Starship Flight 14, showing the upper stage releasing next-generation starlink satellites

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.920
after reaching orbit. The video captures the separation sequence in clear detail.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.800
India today published the release. Elon Musk posted the two words,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.140
SpaceX Talk on X, along with an image or document that appears to preview a presentation.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:44.040
October 1st already delivered three separate orbital missions inside a 13-hour window,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:50.040
including the Crew Dragon capsule grace that reached the station in seven hours and 55 minutes,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.960
It's a new American record.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.660
Work continues on pad 2 at Starbase for upcoming Starship flights.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.480
Basinor reported the post and the surrounding context.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:07.800
A public exchange between a SpaceX AI employee and OpenAI's Tibo Sotio began over Grockbott

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.140
and OpenAI's new dots agents and ended on the topic of compute resources.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:19.120
The SpaceX AI employee closed the thread by noting that only one side actually owns

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:30.500
the hardware. Colossus-1 currently runs 150,000 H100 GPUs, 50,000 H200 GPUs, and 30,000 GB 200

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:44.140
GPUs. Colossus-2 holds 110,000 GB 200 GPUs, and 440,000 GB 300 GPUs, with another 220,000 GB 300 GPUs

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:50.960
expected online shortly. Office Chai documented the exchange. Starlink stated that undisclosed

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.900
satellite maneuvers now represent the largest collision risk for its constellation of more than

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:02.160
11,000 satellites. The company noted that unexpected trajectory changes from other operators

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.320
create the dominant challenge in low-earth orbit. Tesla North covered the statement.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:13.060
SpaceX is moving forward with plans to conduct starship launches from Kennedy Space Center,

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.660
in addition to Starbase.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.220
The effort aims to increase overall launch capacity

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.720
through additional infrastructure.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.420
Aviation Week reported the development.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.080
On the SpaceX lounge subreddit,

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.780
users debated whether Starship could eventually replace Falcon 9

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.960
based on frequency, reliability, and reusability metrics.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.980
The thread compared projected turnaround times

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.760
against current booster flight counts.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.540
A separate thread asked whether SpaceX

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.840
SpaceX has fully mastered Falcon 9 operations by reviewing recent performance data against

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.080
earlier flight history.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.520
Both discussions appear on Reddit.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.200
Starlink opened a beta program that lets property owners and local operators share one

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.120
satellite terminal with nearby users and earn income in return.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:05.540
Apartment complexes, campsites, and event venues are invited to apply through the company website.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.180
Telecom Pepper carried the announcement.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:14.780
NASA astronaut Jessica Mir moved her sleeping bag into a SpaceX dragon capsule after the

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.680
arrival of crew 13 made the station too crowded.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:22.420
The capsule provides 9.3 cubic meters of pressurized volume.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:28.340
Mir posted a photo with the caption, Room With a View, and filmed a short video from inside

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.460
the temporary quarters.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.200
National World reported the arrangement.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.260
Yahoo Finance UK noted the milestone.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:41.620
Stone. NASA and SpaceX now target October 8th for the crew 12 return after 8 months on

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:48.320
the station. The Dragon will perform its deorbit burn and splash down in the Pacific. NASA Space

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:53.560
Flight published the updated schedule. One thing worth watching is that SpaceX can test

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:58.380
on the Echo Star frequencies only until the second stage of the acquisition closes in

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.780
in November, 2027.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.480
The $17 billion spectrum purchase still carries

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.000
a $2.4 billion escrow condition.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.860
Some telecom executives have already

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.900
dismissed the FEMPO cell ground approach

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.280
for dense urban coverage.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.020
Notebook check included those caveats in its coverage.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:20.840
On the AI front, the public spar between SpaceX AI and open

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.560
AI staff highlighted differences in own compute scale.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.160
From an engineering standpoint, the decision

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:33.860
to place the next generation starlink mobile satellites at 326 to 355 kilometers altitude

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:40.500
trades atmospheric drag for lower latency. At these heights residual air density still removes

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.300
a few hundred meters per day from orbital altitude requiring periodic station keeping burns that

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:52.180
consume propellant mass budgeted into each satellite. Lower orbits also reduce the free space

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:58.160
path loss in the link budget, allowing the 150 megabit target with smaller user terminal

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.120
antennas and lower transmit power on the ground.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:06.600
The waiver removing the need for terrestrial spectrum leasing agreements further simplifies

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:12.100
the payload by eliminating coordination hardware that would otherwise add mass and failure

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:12.500
modes.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:19.000
With 15,000 satellites authorized, the constellation can achieve the spatial diversity needed for

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.420
continuous coverage even when individual satellites are temporarily unavailable for station

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.720
keeping or eclipse power management.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.120
The femtocell ground segment then becomes the remaining variable.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:37.000
Each small cell must hand off traffic to the satellite constellation without creating interference

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.540
zones that would force the orbital assets to throttle power.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.000
Solving that interface at scale determines whether the regulatory path translates into

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.880
operational density or remains limited to rural dead zones.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.000
A quick note on the markets.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:57.620
Before we go, watch for further details on the upcoming SpaceX talk that Musk teased,

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.840
and any new footage from ongoing Starship operations at Starbase.

